  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "search_valid_dns",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/dns.c",
    "description": "In DNS reply parsing, `search_valid_dns` can advance `x` to `payload_packet_len-1` after scanning the query name, then unconditionally does `x += 4` and later calls `get16(&x, payload)` for `rsp_type` without revalidating that at least 2 bytes remain. This missing bounds check allows `get16` to read past the heap buffer (2-byte OOB read). The crash occurs in `get16`, but the root cause is incorrect offset/bounds management in `search_valid_dns`.",
    "conditions": "Reach DNS dissector via packet ports (53/5355) with payload length just above DNS header minimum so parsing starts. Provide a packet interpreted as DNS response (`flags` response bit set, counts passing reply validity checks) where the question section is truncated so that after name scan and fixed `x += 4`, `x` is near end-of-payload. Then answer parsing path (`num_answers > 0`) executes and `get16` is called on insufficient remaining bytes, triggering heap OOB read."
  },
